# Difficulty 0 — an eager means takes a difficulty-1 act to 0
#
# move has a base difficulty of 1. The action modus mentis's willingness adds −1 (eager), 0 or +1
# (reluctant); --willingness eager pins the playground's answer, so the walk is difficulty 0 — the ○
# glyph — and succeeds with no roll, `strategy fail-dice` notwithstanding. cli/verb/move/fail.cli is
# the same walk at a willing means, which rolls and misses.
#
# FLAGS: --playground --willingness eager --skip-childhood --debug --seed 42 --no-encounters --auto-dialogue --location-type test --location-id 0 --start-area "Test Field" --period dawn --observe-only "Test Yard"

wait
click menu New
wait mode ProtagonistCreation 20
click continue
wait mode WorldView 60
travel here
wait mode LocationInteraction 60

strategy fail-dice
goal move
advance 12 180

click observe "Test Yard"
choose childhood_memory
advance 12 180
click think "Test Yard"
choose ripelore
advance 12 180

expect ○
expect-not ①

click act 0
choose 0
advance 12 180

expect SUCCESS
expect-not FAILURE
expect-verb move
expect Moved to:
expect-outcome area_move
quit
